{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>However, on the tenth of the month</b> — \"however\" is a restriction: it atones for those who return (in repentance) but does not atone for those who do not return. And there are five afflictions: eating, drinking, washing, anointing, wearing sandals, and marital relations. Corresponding to the five times נפש is written in the portion, and corresponding to the five names that the soul has, and five immersions for the High Priest."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:20:22.414273865Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}